# MSTRMND Core — agent rules

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/MASTER.md` before planning or coding. Hard invariants
there win over anything here.

## Modular abstraction (anti-lock-in)

The intelligence layer must outlive any host, model provider, or vendor SDK.
Hosting is an adapter, exactly like Obsidian or a model provider.

- **Domain code never imports a hosting SDK.** Agents, tools, subagents, skills,
  workflows, and schemas stay platform-agnostic. `@vercel/sandbox`,
  platform-storage clients, and platform-identity clients belong in an adapter
  module and nowhere else.
- **Adapters live at the edge, one file per seam**, and are selected by
  environment variable — not by import site:
  - `mstrmnd-os/agent/sandbox.ts` — sandbox backend (`MSTRMND_SANDBOX`)
  - `mstrmnd-os/agent/lib/model.ts` — model provider (`MSTRMND_PROVIDER`,
    `MSTRMND_MODEL_BASE_URL`)
  - `mstrmnd-os/lib/db.ts` — Postgres (`DATABASE_URL`)
  - `mstrmnd-os/agent/agent.ts` — durability world (`MSTRMND_WORKFLOW_WORLD`)
- **Tools ask the runtime, not the vendor.** Use `ctx.getSandbox()`; do not
  construct a vendor sandbox inside a tool.
- **Every new vendor dependency ships with its non-Vercel path** and a new row
  in `docs/portability.md`. A coupling that cannot be swapped must be named
  there, not left for someone to discover during a migration.
- **The web app must keep building standalone.** Do not remove
  `output: "standalone"` from `mstrmnd-os/next.config.ts`, and do not add build
  steps that only exist on one platform.
- **Clients address a configured base URL.** No deployment domain is hardcoded
  in web or mobile code; the mobile app reads `EXPO_PUBLIC_MSTRMND_API_URL`.
- **Data stays on portable engines.** Standard Postgres over platform-exclusive
  storage; adapters translate vendor shapes into `packages/schemas` types.

## Stack

- pnpm 10+ / Node 20+ (Node 24+ for `mstrmnd-os`) / turbo. Never npm.
- Drive from the repo root with turbo + pnpm filters; do not `cd` into packages
  ad-hoc.
- `mstrmnd-os` is its own pnpm workspace — run its scripts from that directory.

## Verify before declaring done

- `pnpm verify` at the repo root (typecheck + doctrine fixture gate).
- `pnpm typecheck` inside `mstrmnd-os` when that app changed.

## Naming reality

Say scaffold when it is a scaffold and shipped when it is shipped, in docs, PR
descriptions, and `docs/MASTER.md`. Update the MASTER backlog when work lands or
is deliberately deferred.
